  "notes": ["Origin: the gallery floor directly below the painting's viewpoint; +Y runs across the gallery towards the atrium, +X along the gallery edge, Z up; metres.", "Gallery: glass floor (top at z = 0) on steel beams; its edge is the row y = 4.18 with a 1.04 m balustrade, returning along x = -2.16.", "West stair (dog-leg): a broad landscape flight of 14 treads (0.12308 m risers, 0.433 m goings) along x = -4.62..-3.12 rises from the garden at y = 0.32 to a landing at z = -1.3538 (y = 6.382..8.002), solved from the painted nosings (16 px rms); a second flight of 11 treads turns west up to the west gallery wing (x < -5.0), which joins the main gallery by a walkway behind the viewpoint (y < -1.6).", "Garden: the atrium floor at z = -3.2, paved, with planting beds west of, between and east of the stair and path; the round glass table stands on it.", "Envelope: curtain walls on a 2 m module at x = -12.46 / 13.54 and y = -6.0 / 16.0 (transoms at [-3.2, -0.58, 3.32, 7.22]), a glazed roof on a 2 m steel grid at z = 7.22; the conservatory crowns a two-storey glass podium; street trees 8.8 m below reach up past its walls, and far off stands the city.", "The painting draws the chair legs inconsistently (one rises to the seat centre, one stands vertical); the chair is a coherent tall glass chair whose four splayed legs land on the painted feet."],
